<title>USA: Ark. Auth. witholds OK on $29.5 mln airport bonds.</title>
<headline>Ark. Auth. witholds OK on $29.5 mln airport bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $29.5 million bond issue to fund a construction project at Northwest Arkansas Regional Airport failed to win approval from the authority building airport, which said it needs additional information, the Arkansas Democrat-Gazette reported Friday.</p>
<p>The construction project involves paving the runway, taxiway and aprons.</p>
<p>Authority staff members sought approval for the bond offering so that a $22 million contract for paving and lighting could be signed Wednesday with Interstate Highway Construction Co for paving and lighting.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
